Implement mobile-app passkey login without breaking the existing PWA login.

Goal
The PWA keeps its current passkey flow, while the native iOS app can authenticate through ASWebAuthenticationSession for arbitrary self-hosted domains.

Add a mobile auth flow:

1. Add endpoint: GET /api/auth/mobile/start

Accept query params:

callback_scheme=discvault

Optional:

state=<random-client-state>

Behavior:
- Generate a temporary mobile_flow_id.
- Store:
  - mobile_flow_id
  - callback_scheme
  - optional state
  - expiry, e.g. 5 minutes
- Redirect or render the normal login page with the flow ID included, for example:

/login?mobile_flow=<mobile_flow_id>

or, if the app is single-page:

/?mobile_flow=<mobile_flow_id>

2. Keep the existing PWA passkey login unchanged.

Current PWA behavior should remain:

POST /api/auth/login/options
navigator.credentials.get(...)
POST /api/auth/login/verify
return { token, username }
PWA stores token in localStorage

3. Extend the passkey verify request to optionally include mobile_flow.

Example request from frontend:

{
  "credential": { "...": "existing WebAuthn credential payload" },
  "mobile_flow": "abc123"
}

4. Update /api/auth/login/verify

After successful passkey verification:

- If mobile_flow is missing:
  - keep current behavior exactly:

{
  "status": "ok",
  "token": "...",
  "username": "..."
}

- If mobile_flow is present:
  - validate the flow exists and has not expired.
  - create a short-lived one-time code, e.g. expires in 60 seconds.
  - store the code mapped to the authenticated user.
  - delete or mark the mobile flow as used.
  - return a callback URL instead of exposing the long-lived token to the browser page:

{
  "status": "ok",
  "callback_url": "discvault://auth-callback?code=ONE_TIME_CODE&state=OPTIONAL_STATE"
}

The frontend should then redirect:

window.location.href = data.callback_url;

5. Add endpoint: POST /api/auth/mobile/exchange

Request:

{
  "code": "ONE_TIME_CODE"
}

Behavior:
- Validate code exists, unused, and not expired.
- Mark it used or delete it.
- Create/return the normal API token for that user.

Response:

{
  "status": "ok",
  "token": "...",
  "username": "..."
}

6. Security requirements

- Do not put the long-lived API token directly in the custom-scheme callback URL.
- Use a short-lived one-time code.
- One-time code should expire quickly, e.g. 60 seconds.
- Mobile flow ID should expire, e.g. 5 minutes.
- Delete/consume both mobile flow and code after use.
- Only allow expected callback schemes, at minimum:

discvault

- Keep all existing WebAuthn challenge validation exactly as-is:
  - challenge
  - origin
  - RP ID hash
  - signature
  - credential ID
  - sign count

7. Frontend behavior

On login page load:
- Detect mobile_flow in the URL.
- Store it in memory for the login attempt.
- When calling /api/auth/login/verify, include that mobile_flow.
- If response contains callback_url, redirect to it.
- Otherwise keep existing PWA behavior and store token in localStorage.

Pseudo-code:

const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
const mobileFlow = params.get('mobile_flow');

const verifyBody = { credential };
if (mobileFlow) {
  verifyBody.mobile_flow = mobileFlow;
}

const res = await fetch(`${API}/auth/login/verify`, {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify(verifyBody)
});

const data = await res.json();

if (data.callback_url) {
  window.location.href = data.callback_url;
  return;
}

if (data.token) {
  localStorage.setItem('dv_token', data.token);
  init();
}

8. Native app expectation

The iOS app will open:

https://SERVER/api/auth/mobile/start?callback_scheme=discvault

using ASWebAuthenticationSession.

After passkey login, the website redirects to:

discvault://auth-callback?code=ONE_TIME_CODE

The app then calls:

POST https://SERVER/api/auth/mobile/exchange

with the code and stores the returned token in Keychain.

This lets arbitrary self-hosted DiscVault servers use passkeys without requiring each domain to be listed in the iOS app's Associated Domains entitlement.
